  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$6^{x}+8^{x}=10^{x}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^{x}+\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^{x}=1 \\Rightarrow\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^{x}=1-\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^{x}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad 6^{x}+8^{x}=10^{x}$ has exactly one real root\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/XYzjtRkq5Rj3rTShp6C7YHqFdDqnEcZ5j0u66SmkjTU.original.fullsize.png\">",
